## Routing

- Missing repository facts: `explorer`.
- Precise mechanical task with low blast radius: `worker-fast`.
- Clear bounded code or configuration work: `implementer`.
- Unclear cause, environment variance, or repeated failure: `debugger`.
- Cross-system, security, production, concurrency, or major tradeoff: `architect`.
- Meaningful implementation batch or final acceptance: `reviewer`.
- Known deterministic commands and generated config checks: `test-runner`.
- Settled documentation deliverable: `documentation`.

## Escalation

Same worker gets one focused evidence-based correction. Second similar failure routes to
`debugger`; architecture or production-boundary failure routes to `architect`. Reviewer
findings become explicit correction tasks. Orchestrator inspects actual diffs and records
attempts; it never repeats an unchanged failed approach.

## Safety

Read-only agents cannot edit, delegate, or use configured MCP writes. Remote pushes,
force operations, merges, publishing, destructive infrastructure commands, credential
changes, secret access, and production load tests remain denied or approval-gated.
